  "conclusions": [
    "All four recipes selected epoch1 and passed frozen offline eligibility. Lower learning rate improved selected development metrics in both auxiliary configurations.",
    "Removing auxiliary loss slightly worsened selected development Huber at both learning rates. This does not support auxiliary interference as the main remedy, or establish a general advantage to retaining auxiliary loss.",
    "Every recipe later reduced training loss while development loss worsened; gentle learning rate reduced this deterioration over the fixed epochs but did not remove it.",
    "Reused development data and checkpoint/recipe selection preclude an independent offline generalization claim.",
    "Gentle passed its exploratory screen but failed fresh confirmation:46.75 percent winner share and minus0.325 points mean margin. No stronger teacher was established or accepted.",
    "Screens used different seed banks; their difference cannot causally establish auxiliary-loss effects on strength. Terminal-value error and parent agreement do not establish candidate-action ranking quality.",
    "Confirmation intervals permit modest benefit or harm. Failure does not establish equivalence, a weaker model or unsuitable cheap data."
  ],
  "recommendation": "Retain generation3. Before further fit tuning or collection, run a bounded training-only candidate-action diagnostic at fixed outcome-blind positions with fixed supplied candidates and matched belief randomness where valid. Measure correction dispersion, changed choices and preference stability against independent deeper-search samples; teacher preferences are a noisy proxy rather than ground truth. Propose a small searched-action-target pilot only if useful signal appears. Do not open old audit or recycle strength labels. This campaign does not justify architecture expansion or more learning-rate search alone."
